# p5 mcp discover: two stdio servers whose discover answer fx's decoder reads by the raw
# text (p5-mcp-discover-stdio.ts `escaped`, `doubled`). `escaped` lists 2026-07-28 and
# 2025-11-25 each written with an escape: fx compares a version as written (`plainString`,
# src/mcp/core/era.zig:370-377, :425@481104fd), so it lists none fx speaks (retrying).
# `doubled` names `supportedVersions` twice: a field named twice says nothing
# (`objectFields`, src/mcp/protocol/wire.zig:142-146@481104fd), so the answer is no version
# list, a legacy answer, and `initialize` follows (ready). `/mcp list` at 8 s.
fx: homefile .fx/mcp.json p5-mcp-discover-stdio-escaped-profile.json
xfx: homefile .xfx/mcp.json p5-mcp-discover-stdio-escaped-profile.json
gateway p5-mcp-hello.json
wait 8
type /mcp list
key Enter
wait 2
snap list
